%description:
FlatReceiverBase: StochasticErrorModel without any rate

StochasticErrorModel with none of its three rates set cannot compute the packet error rate. The run stops at the first frame with an error that names the error model.

Two ad-hoc IEEE 802.11 hosts, 20 m apart, multicast frames.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib
**.radio.receiver.errorModel.typename = "StochasticErrorModel"
include ../../lib/stochastic-errormodel-80211.ini

%exitcode: 1
%postrun-command: grep -h '<!>' test.out test.err > errors.out || true
%contains: errors.out
Error model inet::physicallayer::StochasticErrorModel cannot provide the packet error rate that the reception decision requires
